### Warehouse CRUD API Tests

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000/api
@authToken = {{login.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### 1. Login to get token
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "username": "admin",
    "password": "admin"
}

### 2. Create a warehouse
POST {{baseUrl}}/warehouses
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
    "name": "East Valley Depot",
    "address": "123 Logistics Blvd, Han City, Pasig City, PH",
    "longitude": 121.086277,
    "latitude": 14.592105, 
    "total_capacity": 10000,
    "created_by": 1
}

### 3. List all active warehouses
GET {{baseUrl}}/warehouses
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 4. Get a single warehouse by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/warehouses/1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 5. Update a warehouse
PUT {{baseUrl}}/warehouses/3
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
    "name": "East Valley Depot",
    "address": "1234 Logistics Blvd, Han City, Pasig City, PH",
    "longitude": 121.086277,
    "latitude": 14.592105, 
    "total_capacity": 10000,
    "updated_by": 1
}

### 6. Deactivate a warehouse
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/warehouses/1/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 7. Reactivate a warehouse
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/warehouses/1/reactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 8. Get all unallocated assets by warehouse
GET {{baseUrl}}/warehouses/1/unallocated
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
